  "term": "melancholic features",
  "definition": "Melancholic features are a depression specifier describing a depressive episode marked by a deeply bleak mood, such as profound hopelessness, despair, moroseness, or feeling emotionally empty. In the supplied source, this subtype is also linked with especially severe negative rumination compared with depression with anxious distress.",
